Coherent changes and task recovery

Install:
  Install the missing bundled skill; preserve installed skill files.
  Add or replace Codex developer_instructions, including when the skill is already installed.

Upgrade:
  Back up and replace the installed skill with bundled files; restore previous skill files if replacement fails.
  Update Codex developer_instructions when the skill is installed; skip both operations when it is missing.

Status:
  Report skill locations based on SKILL.md presence.
  Report whether Codex developer_instructions matches the managed instruction.

Requirements:
  A regular user, AWK and standard file utilities.

Configuration:
  Destination: ~/.agents/skills/coherent-change
  Existing copies at ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/skills/coherent-change are consolidated into links to the destination when skill files are replaced.
  Codex configuration: ${CODEX_HOME:-$HOME/.codex}/config.toml
  developer_instructions = "Read and follow the coherent-change skill before changing code, configuration, or scripts. After context compaction or a handoff, reread it and resume unfinished work."
  Replace the entire developer_instructions value; preserve other settings and back up the configuration before its first change.
